# Build context for services/api/Dockerfile and apps/web/Dockerfile,
# both of which build from the repository root.
#
# Those Dockerfiles copy only: package.json, packages/contracts,
# services/api, apps/web and infra/nginx. Everything excluded below is
# therefore unused by them -- but note that each image reinstalls its own
# dependencies, so excluding node_modules is required for correctness on
# Linux as well as for size (a Windows/macOS node_modules contains
# platform-specific binaries that would break the image).

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Rebuilt inside the image; a stale copy would be shadowed anyway.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore
.github

# The AI service builds from its own context (services/ai) and is never
# copied into the API or web images. This is the largest single exclusion
# here -- it holds the legal corpus and the fine-tuning outputs.
services/ai

# Local state and caches.
.claude
coverage
**/coverage
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.venv
**/.venv

# Secrets must never enter a build context, where they would persist in
# the image layers even if deleted by a later instruction.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Documentation and local uploads are not part of any runtime image.
docs
data/uploads

*.log
.DS_Store
